Dynasty Legacies:
----------

Roman Nostalgia: "Rome is the city of echoes, the city of illusions, and the city of yearning."
- Only for:
   - Non-Romans with Sub-Roman government
   - Mutually exclusive with Despoliation
Level 1: 'Hope for Rome'
   - Reduces frequency of Sub-Roman degradation events
Level 2: 'Protection of Rome'
   - Get a 10-year dynasty modifier blocking most CBs from Roman Empires
   - Unable to promote culture or convert Roman provinces for 30 years if not Roman (dynasty modifier)
   - Your non-Roman vassals may shift towards feuding
Level 3: 'Respect for Rome'
   - Get a 10-year dynasty modifier blocking most CBs from Roman Empires
   - Immediately maximizes non-Roman law in favor of Romans and blocks shifting downwards when your dynasty rules
   - All Roman houses in your polity immediately shift to Faithful level of relations
   - Your non-Roman vassals may shift towards feuding depending on relations (Despoliation always does)
Level 4: 'Faith in Rome'
   - Get a 10-year dynasty modifier blocking most CBs from Roman Empires
   - You adopt the nearest Roman state faith if available, otherwise the closest Emperor's faith, else the majority faith of Romans in your realm
   - Your polity adopts the nearest Roman state faith if available, otherwise the closest Emperor's faith, else the majority faith of Romans in your realm
   - Your non-Roman vassals may shift towards feuding (zealous house heads not of a Righteous Roman faith always do)
Level 5: 'Emulation of Rome'
   - Cost to hybridize & acceptance to hybridize with Roman culture sharply reduced if a culture in your realm still has "Romance/Hellenic Culture" (only applies once)
   - Unlocks "Romanitas" Dynastic Legacy
   - Your non-Roman vassals may shift towards feuding
   - Change COA frame to match Roman culture of your realm [IS THIS ACTUALLY POSSIBLE?]
